> To be sure, a caught rocket is not a utopia. The Culture runs on physics we don't have and on machine benevolence nobody knows how to engineer; Banks could simply decree that his Minds were kind. Musk's calendar is famously elastic: he promised a million robotaxis by 2020 and cargo ships on Mars by 2022, and both dates came and went. To some, there is an awkward fact at the center of his enthusiasm. The Culture has no billionaires. Banks himself wondered aloud how his libertarian admirers had managed to miss that his paradise abolished private property.
> 
> Musk, though, has not missed it. He predicts that, with enough AI and robotics, money "will stop being relevant." In a civilization so rich that money has withered away, nobody is a billionaire, and nobody needs to be.
